    <h2 id="about-h">About</h2>
    <p>I work where machine learning meets application security: deciding what to trust, and being able to prove it. I got here almost by chance and stayed because the problems are hard in the right way. Lately most of my building and experimenting has been with agentic AI and RAG systems: agents that watch data, read documents, and act on what they find.</p>
    <p>Recent work: a risk-scoring engine that re-ranks SAST, DAST, and SCA findings by deployment context (LightGBM, XGBoost, SHAP explanations); Codegate, a conformal risk-control gate that sends AI-generated code to an LLM reviewer only when static analysis can't clear it; and agentic RAG systems that forecast burn rates and read policy documents for compliance.</p>
    <p>At VIT Vellore I'm the Head of Events for the IEEE-SSIT chapter, where I've planned and hosted tech talks with industry leaders and overnight hackathons with 800+ participants. From the other side of the table: top 40 in ZS Campus Beats (India-wide), 5th overall at HackX 3.0, top 20 at DevSpace.</p>
    <p>Fuel of choice: Shawarma.</p>
  </div>
</section>
